        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9015024?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Corrected the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Guides/Constraint_validation#semantic_input_types\" rel=\"nofollow\">Semantic input types</a>  section to clarify that the multiple attribute applies to email inputs but not url inputs.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The documentation previously stated both email and url inputs support the multiple attribute for comma-separated lists.  However, according to the HTML Standard, the multiple attribute is not supported for <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;input type=\"url\"&gt;</code>. This update aligns the guide with the specification.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42005.\">Fixes</span>  <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3639467668\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42005\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42005/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42005\">#42005</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42023",
            "title": "Remove incorrect claim that URL inputs support 'multiple' attribute",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-19T21:07:40.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-19T18:59:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "asell22",
