        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220878433?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds clarification to the Return value section of the scripting.executeScript() documentation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The issue (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3618228527\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41916\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41916/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41916\">#41916</a>) points out that users may think Promises cannot be returned, since the structured-clone documentation doesn’t mention them. This update explains that Firefox awaits returned Promises and uses their resolved values, matching Chrome’s behavior.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related issues</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41916.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3618228527\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41916\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41916/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41916\">#41916</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41932",
            "title": "docs: clarify promise behavior in executeScript return value (#41916)",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-17T21:24:49.000Z",
